    {
      "id": 200,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 30, "w": 24, "h": 4 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**How to read** &nbsp;·&nbsp; Top row = state *right now* (30d window). &nbsp;·&nbsp; When *Error Budget Remaining* < 20% → we freeze risky deploys and prioritise reliability. &nbsp;·&nbsp; A sustained burn rate > 1 = the budget runs out before the window ends.\n\n**SLO assumptions** (to be formalised in an ADR): availability 99.5% (no 5xx), latency 99.5% < 500 ms, business < 1% lost reservations — rolling 30-day window. The latency threshold is tied to the `le=0.5` bucket boundary; changing it requires adding a new boundary to `management.metrics.distribution.slo` in `application.yml`."
      }
    }
